{
  "_comment": "Decisive end-to-end test of the JOINT shape+rotation solve, and of the turn-angle law that governs it. N=6 (cheap) at a 6 HOUR arc, because the measured CRLB says a 3600 s arc turns the formation only 15 deg and cannot separate an arc-constant shape offset from an arc-constant rotation at all (penalty 9.9x), while 21600 s turns it 90 deg and brings the penalty to 2.1x. Also switches on the cone terminal layout and ISL delay-bias self-calibration, which are the two config-only shape improvements already implemented and measured. Expectation to be tested: shape well below the 4.1 m of run16, and a rotation correction that actually reduces the rotation error instead of leaking shape into it.",
  "scenario": {
    "name": "smoke_parallel",
    "nTowers": 5,
    "nSpaceAssets": 3,
    "nReceivers": 4
  },
  "simulation": {
    "duration_s": 120
  },
